summary: D580 net.connect_within over hosted/events connects within a limit and with none, is refused at once by a port nothing listens on, and fails timed_out against a peer that never answers once the limit has passed, its fibre parked on the loop with the limit as its deadline while another fibre sleeps and counts, after which a connection is unharmed; the peer is a full listener, of backlog 0 on Linux and 1 on Darwin, and fe80::2%lo0 on FreeBSD
